Concrete class extending an abstract class and implementing an interface

// Abstract class - Defines common properties & behaviors
abstract class Animal {
    String name;

    Animal(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    abstract void makeSound(); // Abstract method

    void sleep() { // Concrete method
        System.out.println(name + " is sleeping.");
    }
}

// Interface - Defines a contract for actions
interface Swimmable {
    void swim();
}

// Dog extends Animal (inherits behavior) and implements Swimmable (adds ability)
class Dog extends Animal implements Swimmable {
    Dog(String name) {
        super(name);
    }

    @Override
    void makeSound() {
        System.out.println(name + " barks.");
    }

    @Override
    public void swim() {
        System.out.println(name + " is swimming.");
    }
}

// Main Class
public class OOPExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Dog dog = new Dog("Buddy");
        dog.makeSound();
        dog.sleep();
        dog.swim();
    }
}



# Vehicle System
    Abstract Class Vehicle: Defines a template for all vehicles.
    Interface FuelConsumption: Defines a contract for fuel efficiency.
    Concrete Class Car: Implements both.

Code Implementation

// Abstract class with common properties and methods
abstract class Vehicle {
    String brand;
    int speed;

    // Constructor
    Vehicle(String brand, int speed) {
        this.brand = brand;
        this.speed = speed;
    }

    // Abstract method (to be implemented by subclasses)
    abstract void start();

    // Concrete method
    void stop() {
        System.out.println(brand + " has stopped.");
    }
}

// Interface defining fuel efficiency behavior
interface FuelConsumption {
    double calculateFuelEfficiency(); // Abstract method
}

// Concrete class extending an abstract class and implementing an interface
class Car extends Vehicle implements FuelConsumption {
    int fuelCapacity; // in liters

    // Constructor
    Car(String brand, int speed, int fuelCapacity) {
        super(brand, speed);
        this.fuelCapacity = fuelCapacity;
    }

    // Implement abstract method from Vehicle
    @Override
    void start() {
        System.out.println(brand + " car is starting at speed: " + speed + " km/h");
    }

    // Implement method from FuelConsumption interface
    @Override
    public double calculateFuelEfficiency() {
        return speed * 0.2; // Example calculation
    }
}

// Main class to demonstrate the implementation
public class OOPExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Car myCar = new Car("Toyota", 100, 50);

        myCar.start();
        System.out.println("Fuel efficiency: " + myCar.calculateFuelEfficiency() + " km/l");
        myCar.stop();
    }
}

Explanation

    Vehicle (Abstract Class)
        Has common properties (brand, speed).
        Contains an abstract method start() that must be implemented in subclasses.
        Has a concrete method stop() that prints a message.

    FuelConsumption (Interface)
        Defines a contract with calculateFuelEfficiency().
        Does not have instance variables or implemented methods (except default methods in Java 8+).

    Car (Concrete Class)
        Extends Vehicle → Must implement start().
        Implements FuelConsumption → Must implement calculateFuelEfficiency().
        Defines a constructor and uses super() to call Vehicle constructor.

    Main Class (OOPExample)
        Creates an instance of Car.
        Calls the implemented methods to demonstrate abstraction and interface usage.

Output

Toyota car is starting at speed: 100 km/h
Fuel efficiency: 20.0 km/l
Toyota has stopped.



# Hospital Management System
Concepts Covered:

    Interface HospitalStaff: Defines common behaviors for all hospital staff.
    Multiple Implementations: Doctor and Nurse classes implement the interface.
    Polymorphism: The interface is used as a reference type.

Code Implementation

// Interface defining the behavior of hospital staff
interface HospitalStaff {
    void checkIn();   // Common method for all staff
    void performDuties(); // Role-specific duties
}

// Doctor class implementing HospitalStaff interface
class Doctor implements HospitalStaff {
    private String name;
    private String specialization;

    // Constructor
    public Doctor(String name, String specialization) {
        this.name = name;
        this.specialization = specialization;
    }

    // Implementing interface methods
    @Override
    public void checkIn() {
        System.out.println("Dr. " + name + " has checked into the hospital.");
    }

    @Override
    public void performDuties() {
        System.out.println("Dr. " + name + " is treating patients in " + specialization + " department.");
    }
}

// Nurse class implementing HospitalStaff interface
class Nurse implements HospitalStaff {
    private String name;
    private int experience;

    // Constructor
    public Nurse(String name, int experience) {
        this.name = name;
        this.experience = experience;
    }

    // Implementing interface methods
    @Override
    public void checkIn() {
        System.out.println("Nurse " + name + " has checked into the hospital.");
    }

    @Override
    public void performDuties() {
        System.out.println("Nurse " + name + " is administering medication with " + experience + " years of experience.");
    }
}

// Main class to test the hospital system
public class HospitalSystem {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Using the interface as a reference
        HospitalStaff doctor = new Doctor("Rajesh", "Cardiology");
        HospitalStaff nurse = new Nurse("Priya", 5);

        // Calling methods
        doctor.checkIn();
        doctor.performDuties();
        System.out.println();
        nurse.checkIn();
        nurse.performDuties();
    }
}

Explanation

    Interface HospitalStaff
        Defines common methods checkIn() and performDuties(), ensuring all hospital staff implement them.

    Class Doctor
        Implements HospitalStaff and defines doctor-specific behavior in performDuties().

    Class Nurse
        Implements HospitalStaff and defines nurse-specific duties.

    Polymorphism in main
        Uses the HospitalStaff interface to refer to both Doctor and Nurse objects.
        Demonstrates flexibility in handling different staff types.

Output

Dr. Rajesh has checked into the hospital.
Dr. Rajesh is treating patients in Cardiology department.

Nurse Priya has checked into the hospital.
Nurse Priya is administering medication with 5 years of experience.